    Res Partner Views — account_payment_followup Module (PF-001 / PF-005)
    =====================================================================

    Extensions to the core ``res.partner`` form, list (tree) and search
    views to surface follow-up state information alongside a dedicated
    "Follow-ups" notebook page that consolidates aging buckets, smart
    buttons, and quick actions.

    Implements:
      - PF-001 Scenarios 1-5: Follow-up level configuration — exposes the
        currently-applicable ``followup_level_id`` and
        ``followup_next_action_date`` on the partner form so accountants
        can verify which level is active and when the next action is due.
      - PF-005 Scenarios 1-6: Overdue calculation — surfaces
        ``has_overdue_invoices``, ``max_days_overdue``, ``total_overdue``,
        and the five aging buckets (``aging_bucket_current``,
        ``aging_bucket_1_30``, ``aging_bucket_31_60``, ``aging_bucket_61_90``,
        ``aging_bucket_90_plus``) on the partner form, list columns, and
        search filters so users can triage and group receivables by
        aging severity.

    Inheritance (R-03):
      - ``base.view_partner_form``   — adds a smart button + a
                                       "Follow-ups" notebook page.
      - ``base.view_partner_tree``   — appends four optional (hidden by
                                       default) columns for AR triage.
      - ``base.view_res_partner_filter`` — appends filters and a group-by
                                           option.

    External ID Resolution:
      The ``base.*`` External IDs are guaranteed to be registered at the
      time this file loads because ``base`` is a transitive dependency
      via both ``account`` and ``mail`` declared in ``__manifest__.py``.

    Group Gating:
      All new UI surfaces are gated by
      ``groups="account.group_account_invoice,account.group_account_readonly"``
      so that accountants (read-write) and auditors (read-only) see the
      follow-up fields on a Community Edition install, while other users
      experience the standard partner form unchanged.

    Rules Compliance (AAP §0.7):
      - R-01: No cross-module references; only references core
              (``base.*``) and installed dependency groups (``account.*``).
      - R-02: No Enterprise module references (account_followup,
              account_reports, account_accountant are absent).
      - R-03: Every record uses ``inherit_id``; no net-new view definitions.
      - R-05: All fields referenced are either pre-existing on core
              ``res.partner`` (``currency_id``, ``is_company``,
              ``customer_rank``) or computed / relational fields added
              via ``_inherit`` in ``models/res_partner.py``.
      - Odoo 19.0 conventions: ``invisible="..."`` (not ``<attrs>``),
        ``<list>`` (not ``<tree>``), ``column_invisible`` for hidden
        list columns, ``optional="hidden"`` for toggleable columns.
-->
<odoo>
    <data>

        <!-- ================================================================
             SECTION 1: PARTNER FORM VIEW — FOLLOW-UP EXTENSIONS
             Model: res.partner
             Inherits: base.view_partner_form
             =================================================================
             Two injections:

               1. A smart button in the form's ``button_box`` that
                  navigates to the partner's follow-up history records.
                  Hidden when ``followup_history_count == 0`` so partners
                  who have never been dunned do not carry an empty
                  counter.

               2. A new "Follow-ups" notebook page showing the partner's
                  current follow-up status (level, next action date,
                  overdue flag), the total overdue amount, the five
                  aging buckets, and a "Send Follow-up Now" action
                  button for on-demand dunning.

             The page is gated by ``not is_company and not customer_rank``
             so it appears only for entities that can realistically carry
             receivables (companies OR any partner flagged as a customer
             via ``customer_rank``). Individual contacts without customer
             status do not see the page.
             ================================================================ -->

        <record id="view_partner_form_followup" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">res.partner.form.followup</field>
            <field name="model">res.partner</field>
            <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.view_partner_form"/>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <!-- Smart button: Follow-up History count -->
                <xpath expr="//div[@name='button_box']" position="inside">
                    <button name="action_view_followup_history"
                            type="object"
                            class="oe_stat_button"
                            icon="fa-history"
                            invisible="followup_history_count == 0"
                            groups="account.group_account_invoice,account.group_account_readonly">
                        <field name="followup_history_count"
                               widget="statinfo"
                               string="Follow-up History"/>
                    </button>
                </xpath>

                <!-- Follow-ups notebook page -->
                <xpath expr="//notebook" position="inside">
                    <page id="followup_page"
                          name="followup"
                          string="Follow-ups"
                          invisible="not is_company and not customer_rank"
                          groups="account.group_account_invoice,account.group_account_readonly">
                        <!-- Row 1: Current Status + Total Overdue -->
                        <group>
                            <group string="Current Status"
                                   name="followup_status_group">
                                <field name="followup_level_id"/>
                                <field name="followup_next_action_date"/>
                                <field name="has_overdue_invoices"/>
                                <field name="max_days_overdue"/>
                            </group>
                            <group string="Total Overdue"
                                   name="followup_total_group">
                                <!--
                                    Issue #23 fix: ``decoration-danger``
                                    flips the total to red whenever the
                                    partner carries any 90+ aging
                                    balance — collections-industry
                                    convention for severe aging.
                                -->
                                <field name="total_overdue"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                                       decoration-danger="aging_bucket_90_plus &gt; 0"/>
                                <field name="currency_id" invisible="1"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>
                        <!-- Row 2: Aging Buckets (two columns) -->
                        <group string="Aging Buckets"
                               name="followup_aging_group">
                            <group>
                                <field name="aging_bucket_current"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"/>
                                <field name="aging_bucket_1_30"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                                       string="1-30 Days Overdue"/>
                                <field name="aging_bucket_31_60"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                                       string="31-60 Days Overdue"/>
                            </group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="aging_bucket_61_90"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                                       string="61-90 Days Overdue"/>
                                <!--
                                    Issues #23, #24, #25 fix:
                                      * ``string="90+ Days Overdue"``
                                        replaces the prior label
                                        ``"Over 90 Days Overdue"`` so
                                        the label fits on a single line
                                        (visual rhythm match with the
                                        sibling labels above) AND
                                        matches the form-level label on
                                        ``account.followup.line``
                                        (terminology consistency across
                                        views — see also list column
                                        header ``"90+ Days"`` on the
                                        followup line list).
                                      * ``decoration-danger`` paints the
                                        90+ bucket red whenever it is
                                        positive — the universal
                                        collections-industry signal
                                        for severe aging.
                                -->
                                <field name="aging_bucket_90_plus"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                                       string="90+ Days Overdue"
                                       decoration-danger="aging_bucket_90_plus &gt; 0"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>
                        <!-- Row 3: Action button "Send Follow-up Now"
                             Invisible when partner has no follow-up
                             level or no overdue invoices. Requires
                             explicit confirmation before dispatch. -->
                        <group>
                            <button name="action_send_followup_now"
                                    type="object"
                                    string="Send Follow-up Now"
                                    class="btn-primary"
                                    invisible="not followup_level_id or not has_overdue_invoices"
                                    confirm="This will send the follow-up email for the current level. Continue?"
                                    groups="account.group_account_invoice"/>
                        </group>
                    </page>
                </xpath>
            </field>
        </record>

        <!-- ================================================================
             SECTION 2: PARTNER LIST (TREE) VIEW — FOLLOW-UP COLUMNS
             Model: res.partner
             Inherits: base.view_partner_tree
             =================================================================
             Appends four optional columns to the core partner list:

               - total_overdue       (Monetary, with sum aggregation)
               - followup_level_id   (Many2one)
               - max_days_overdue    (Integer)
               - currency_id         (column_invisible — needed by the
                                      monetary widget only)

             All columns are ``optional="hidden"`` so they are NOT shown
             by default — users opt in via the list's column picker.
             This prevents extra column-width pressure for users who are
             not focused on AR and avoids redundant rendering for
             partners with no receivable activity.

             The columns are appended at the END of the list via
             ``<xpath expr="//list" position="inside">`` because:
               (a) the core list root is always ``<list>`` in Odoo 19;
               (b) this survives re-ordering of core fields across
                   minor Odoo versions;
               (c) ``optional="hidden"`` columns added at the end of
                   the list is the canonical OCA pattern.
             ================================================================ -->

        <record id="view_partner_tree_followup" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">res.partner.list.followup</field>
            <field name="model">res.partner</field>
            <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.view_partner_tree"/>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <xpath expr="//list" position="inside">
                    <field name="total_overdue"
                           widget="monetary"
                           options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                           optional="hidden"
                           sum="Total Overdue"/>
                    <field name="followup_level_id"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="max_days_overdue"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="currency_id"
                           column_invisible="True"/>
                </xpath>
            </field>
        </record>

        <!-- ================================================================
             SECTION 3: PARTNER SEARCH VIEW — FOLLOW-UP FILTERS
             Model: res.partner
             Inherits: base.view_res_partner_filter
             =================================================================
             Adds two ad-hoc filters and one group-by option to the core
             partner search view:

               - "Has Overdue Invoices" — domain filter on the stored,
                 indexed ``has_overdue_invoices`` Boolean. Fast because
                 the field is computed-and-stored with an index (see
                 models/res_partner.py).

               - "At Follow-up Level" — domain filter returning partners
                 with a non-null ``followup_level_id``.

               - "Follow-up Level" (group-by) — groups the search result
                 by the stored Many2one ``followup_level_id``.

             The filters are inserted ``before`` the stable "inactive"
             filter anchor (the pattern used by the core ``account``
             module at ``addons/account/views/partner_view.xml``), and
             the group-by option is inserted ``inside`` the existing
             core ``group_by`` group so the merged search view preserves
             a single, schema-valid element ordering.
             ================================================================ -->

        <record id="view_res_partner_filter_followup" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">res.partner.search.followup</field>
            <field name="model">res.partner</field>
            <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.view_res_partner_filter"/>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <xpath expr="//filter[@name='inactive']" position="before">
                    <filter name="has_overdue_invoices"
                            string="Has Overdue Invoices"
                            domain="[('has_overdue_invoices', '=', True)]"/>
                    <filter name="at_followup_level"
                            string="At Follow-up Level"
                            domain="[('followup_level_id', '!=', False)]"/>
                    <separator/>
                </xpath>
                <xpath expr="//group[@name='group_by']" position="inside">
                    <filter name="group_followup_level"
                            string="Follow-up Level"
                            context="{'group_by': 'followup_level_id'}"/>
                </xpath>
            </field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
